---
/**
 * The About page.
 *
 * Rewritten because the original leaned on `prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert`, and
 * `@tailwindcss/typography` is not installed — so those three classes matched no CSS at all. The
 * page rendered as one undifferentiated wall of text: no bullets, no space between paragraphs,
 * and in-prose links styled the same as the text around them. It also had no `h2` anywhere, which
 * left a 400-word page with no outline for a crawler to read.
 *
 * Everything here is built from the site's own utility classes instead, the same way every other
 * page is. The guides get their `.prose` block because their body is Markdown that has to be
 * styled generically; this page is hand-written markup and does not need it.
 */
import { url } from '@/lib/url';
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/lib/site';
import { abs, breadcrumbs, ids } from '@/lib/schema';

const title = 'About SellerWala';
const description =
	'SellerWala makes free, browser-only tools for Indian sellers: crop and sort Meesho labels, and find your real profit. No login, no uploads, no watermarks.';

const tools = [
	{
		path: '/tools/meesho-label-cropper',
		name: 'The label cropper',
		detail:
			'Crops the invoice away, fits the label to your printer, and sorts the batch the way you actually pack — with a pick list of how many of each SKU to pull off the shelf.',
	},
	{
		path: '/tools/meesho-profit-calculator',
		name: 'The profit calculator',
		detail:
			'Reads your payment file and works out what you really earned — after cost of goods, ads, returns, and the rent and salaries no marketplace has ever heard of — down to the margin on each individual SKU.',
	},
];

const principles = [
	{
		claim: 'Nothing you add leaves your device.',
		detail:
			"There is no server that processes your files. Cropping, sorting, PDF building and every profit calculation happen locally in your browser, using code that runs on your machine — not ours. That matters twice over here: one file holds your customers' addresses, the other holds your entire revenue.",
	},
	{
		claim: 'No account, ever.',
		detail:
			"There's nothing to sign up for and nothing to forget a password for. Open a tool, use it, close the tab.",
	},
	{
		claim: 'Free forever, funded by ads.',
		detail:
			'Advertising is placed away from the upload, preview, and download flow, so it never gets in the way of actually getting the work done.',
	},
];

const schema = [
	breadcrumbs(Astro.site, [{ name: 'About', path: '/about' }]),
	{
		'@context': 'https://schema.org',
		'@type': 'AboutPage',
		name: title,
		description,
		url: abs('/about', Astro.site),
		// The page is about the organisation, so it says so rather than re-describing the brand.
		mainEntity: { '@id': ids.organization(Astro.site) },
		isPartOf: { '@id': ids.website(Astro.site) },
		inLanguage: 'en-IN',
	},
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
		<h1 data-reveal class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">About {SITE.name}</h1>

		<p data-reveal class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-pretty text-muted-foreground">
			{SITE.name} exists because running a Meesho shop means doing two thankless jobs over and over.
			The first is getting orders out of the door. The second is finding out whether any of it made
			money.
		</p>

		<h2 data-reveal class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The problem</h2>
		<p data-reveal class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			Meesho — like most Indian marketplaces — exports shipping labels with a tax invoice glued to
			the same page, in whatever order your orders happened to sync in. So before you can print
			anything you are cutting, re-sorting, and wasting label stock.
		</p>
		<p data-reveal class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			Then, at the other end, the supplier panel will not tell you whether the month worked. It
			reports what it paid you, and stops there — which is revenue, not profit. It has no idea what
			your products cost, what you spend on packaging, or what your rent is.
		</p>

		<h2 data-reveal class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
			Two tools, two ends of the same order
		</h2>
		<dl class="mt-6 space-y-4">
			{
				tools.map((tool) => (
					<div data-reveal class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5">
						<dt class="font-semibold">
							<a
								href={url(tool.path)}
								class="text-primary underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:underline"
							>
								{tool.name}
							</a>
						</dt>
						<dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{tool.detail}</dd>
					</div>
				))
			}
		</dl>

		<h2 data-reveal class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What we will not do</h2>
		<dl class="mt-6 space-y-4">
			{
				principles.map((principle) => (
					<div data-reveal class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-5">
						<dt class="font-semibold">{principle.claim}</dt>
						<dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">{principle.detail}</dd>
					</div>
				))
			}
		</dl>

		<h2 data-reveal class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What's next</h2>
		<p data-reveal class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			Both tools start with Meesho, because that is the marketplace we know best. Amazon and
			Flipkart label cropping are on the roadmap — the underlying engine was built to take more
			marketplaces, so what is left is the per-marketplace detail rather than a rewrite. The{' '}
			<a href={url('/faq')} class="font-medium text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">FAQ</a>
			{' '}covers the rest, and the{' '}
			<a href={url('/guides')} class="font-medium text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">
				guides
			</a>
			{' '}go deeper on printing, couriers and payments.
		</p>

		<div
			data-reveal
			class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-stretch justify-center gap-2.5 sm:flex-row sm:items-center"
		>
			<a
				href={url('/tools/meesho-label-cropper')}
				class="press inline-flex min-h-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-primary px-6 text-base font-semibold text-primary-foreground shadow-sm transition-transform duration-150 hover:scale-[1.02] active:scale-[0.98]"
			>
				Open the Label Cropper
			</a>
			<a
				href={url('/tools/meesho-profit-calculator')}
				class="press inline-flex min-h-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-border bg-background px-6 text-base font-semibold transition-colors hover:border-primary/40 hover:text-primary"
			>
				Open the Profit Calculator
			</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
